WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.667
-I am and have always been
a normal homosexual man

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:07.200
who does all the normal things
normal homosexual men do.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.167
-Like what?
-Well, I'll tell you.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.267
♪ I wake up, drink my coffee ♪

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.801
♪ Have brunch around 11 ♪

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:20.367
♪ Walk my Bichon-Frisé,
then nap till half past seven ♪

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.534
♪ A night out at the symphony ♪

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.901
♪ Such elegance, what poise? ♪

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:28.968
♪ Or maybe I'll just stay at
home with my two Sewer Boys ♪

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:30.133
-What?

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:33.334
-♪ The answer
is perfectly clear ♪

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:39.400
♪ It's a gay old life
being queer ♪

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.634
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.200
We're here with Nathan Lane.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.634
That was a clip
from "Dicks: The Musical."

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:48.934
-Yes.
-And this is a story

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.767
about separated twins.

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:54.901
-Yes. It's a --
it is a deeply silly,

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:56.267
satirical, absurdist,

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:59.133
R-rated queer musical
based on "The Parent Trap."

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.868
-There we go.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:04.167
-And, you know,
it's not for everybody.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:06.601
It's for -- It's for the gay
and the --

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.200
and the --
and the open minded.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.634
It's for the demented
and depraved.

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.634
It is the cinematic enema

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:18.968
America has been
so desperate for.

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:23.968
So, you know, I would say have
an edible or two and run,

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:28.667
don't walk to catch
some "Dicks: The Musical."

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:32.734
-[ Laughs ] Now, in the clip,
you referenced the Sewer Boys,

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:36.133
and I'm glad you brought them

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:38.200
because we don't see them
in the clip.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.400
-I know
-And I -- they really,

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.734
no offense,
they kind of steal the show.

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:43.934
-Oh, totally.

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:45.267
And it's all anyone's
talking about

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:46.868
aside from Taylor Swift,
the Sewer Boys.

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:48.734
-So, do you want to set up
the Sewer Boys?

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:53.501
-The Sewer Boys are -- are --
are these creatures

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:56.434
I captured, obviously
in the sewer,

00:01:56.434 --> 00:02:00.267
and I take them into my home
and they're like rescue dogs

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.601
and I keep them in a cage
in my living room.

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:06.534
[ Clears throat ] And I feed
them sort of like a mother bird.

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:10.200
They like deli meat,
so I chew up ham

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.868
and I spit it into their mouths.

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:14.334
You know, like their mother.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.334
-When doing that is
an award-winning actor...

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:17.467
-Yes.
-...what's going

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:18.801
through your head?

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:22.934
-Well, you know, when -- when we
talked about this,

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:25.467
at first when
they brought them out,

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:28.534
most of the budget went into
these puppets, by the way.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:31.267
And when they brought them out,
I said, this looks like someone

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:34.200
stole a Halloween display
from Walmart.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.334
This can't possibly
be the real thing.

00:02:36.334 --> 00:02:37.968
And they said,
"Oh, no, don't worry,

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:39.300
we're just getting started."

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.801
And then they put
diapers on them.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:43.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.167
So these are my --
my Sewer Boys.

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:48.234
-Alright.
There's...

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:54.334
-And -- and as you can see,
they -- they -- they --

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:55.400
they wear diapers.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.901
In the sewer,
they didn't have to.

00:02:56.901 --> 00:03:00.834
-I want to tell you,
it's a wonderful thing.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.501
First of all, there's so much
heavier than they look.

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:06.434
-Right? Me too.
-And...

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:08.934
-Oh, they -- they wear
ankle bracelets as well.

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:10.534
-And their -- their names.

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:12.534
I think this is the litmus test.

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:14.501
They're disgusting,
aren't they?

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:16.334
I think the litmus test
for this movie

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:19.634
are the names of the Sewer Boys
are Backpack and whisper.

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:25.033
-Now -- now, if you think
that's funny,

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.567
this is the movie for you.

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:30.000
And and if not, then you should
probably stay home

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.801
and watch that marathon
of "Blue Bloods."

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:33.234
-Yes.

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:34.801
Now, I do want
to say one thing before.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.267
You were very nice and said

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:37.667
let's bring the Sewer Boys
on the show.

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:38.667
-Yeah.
-And we had to send --

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:39.701
because they're very heavy.

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:41.000
We couldn't ask you
to bring them,

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.334
so we spent a production
assistant.

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:43.701
-They don't really live with me.

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:45.267
-Yeah, that's true.
-Yeah.

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:47.100
They were --
they were at age A24.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.200
-Yeah. So we sent a production
assistant to get them.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.801
-Yeah. And what happened?
-And she brought them

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:52.634
on the subway like this?

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:54.701
-No.
-And guess what?

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.300
No one batted an eye.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.534
New York City, baby.

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:02.067
Nathan Lane, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:06.300
"Dicks: The Musical"
opens nationwide this Friday,

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.634
and the soundtrack
is available now.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:10.267
We'll be right back
with Lauren Schuker Blum

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:11.467
and Rebecca Angelo.

